# Entry Main: the tail of a return supplies the described result fields in order (the book #structure-result; step
# 21.7 K3, part 2). D describes `return:` with `int: x`, `int: y`; C returns the tail `7 9`. The call answers one
# new Structure: x 7, y 9. observed 79.
@: result 0
int: observed 0
D:
    return:
        int: x
        int: y
    end: return
    C:
        return: 7 9
    end: C
end: D
---
Main:
    node\result := D\C()
    node\observed := node\result\x * 10 + node\result\y
